From: qdEngine English patch <patch@qdengine.local>
Subject: [PATCH] qdengine: full redraw on interface screen change + button init

The main menu draws volume sliders (music/zvuk) each frame because they are
linked to option_id values, but the background (fon.tga) and 800x600 button
QDAs only register screen regions on the first full redraw. Without a game-level
fullscreen invalidation after select_screen(), later frames repaint only the
slider strips and the rest of the menu stays black.

Also force qdInterfaceButton::init() to activate state 0 so button animations
are referenced before the first redraw.

Apply on top of scummvm/qdengine_nested_loose_files.patch when building ScummVM.

diff --git a/engines/qdengine/qdcore/qd_interface_button.cpp b/engines/qdengine/qdcore/qd_interface_button.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/engines/qdengine/qdcore/qd_interface_button.cpp
+++ b/engines/qdengine/qdcore/qd_interface_button.cpp
@@ -186,8 +186,11 @@ bool qdInterfaceButton::init(bool is_game_active) {
 		p->set_state_mode(qdInterfaceElementState::DEFAULT_MODE);
 	}
 
-	if (_cur_state != -1)
-		return set_state(get_state(_cur_state));
+	if (num_states() > 0) {
+		if (_cur_state < 0)
+			_cur_state = 0;
+		return activate_state(_cur_state);
+	}
 
 	return true;
 }
diff --git a/engines/qdengine/qdcore/qd_interface_dispatcher.cpp b/engines/qdengine/qdcore/qd_interface_dispatcher.cpp
index 3333333..4444444 100644
--- a/engines/qdengine/qdcore/qd_interface_dispatcher.cpp
+++ b/engines/qdengine/qdcore/qd_interface_dispatcher.cpp
@@ -154,6 +154,9 @@ bool qdInterfaceDispatcher::select_screen(const char *screen_name, bool lock_reso
 			_cur_screen->lock_resources();
 	}
 
+	if (qdGameDispatcher *gdp = qdGameDispatcher::get_dispatcher())
+		gdp->toggle_full_redraw();
+
 	_need_full_redraw = true;
 
 	return true;